 "equipment_type": "Lighting gateway (DALI-2 to Modbus)",
 "applies_to": "Intesis Modbus Server - DALI with one (0640000, RTU + TCP) or two (1280000, TCP only) DALI channels, Modbus Addresses parameter set to Fixed; user manual r1.2 (09/2021).",
 "summary": "Gateway that exposes DALI / DALI-2 control gear on one or two DALI lines as Modbus holding registers. Addresses follow fixed formulas: per ballast short address (100 registers each), per DALI group (from 6400) and broadcast (from 6800), plus a 7000 offset for the second line. Signals cover levels, on/off, step, scenes, fade and limit settings, status and failure bits.",
 "transport": [
  "RTU",
  "TCP"
 ],
 "defaults": {
  "unit_id": null,
  "baud": null,
  "parity": null,
  "data_bits": null,
  "stop_bits": null,
  "tcp_port": 502
 },
 "addressing": {
  "convention": "parameter-derived",
  "note": "Address = 7000 x channel + 100 x short address + signal (ballasts), 7000 x line + 20 x group + 6400..6415 (groups), 7000 x line + 6800..6815 (broadcast). The manual states the result is in link-layer format with the first register at 0, so it is the wire address. Only short address 0, group 0 and two broadcast signals of channel 0 are listed."
 },
 "default_word_order": null,
 "firmware": null,
 "source": {
  "title": "Intesis Modbus Server - DALI (DALI-2) User Manual",
  "doc_number": "User Manual r1.2 EN (page headers read r1.1)",
  "revision_date": "2021-09",
  "url": "https://cdn.chipkin.com/assets/uploads/2022/Feb/user-manual-inmbsdalxxx0000_17-21-45-17.pdf",
  "unofficial": true,
  "pages": "p. 10 (Modbus interface), pp. 11-18 (single device map), pp. 19-20 (groups), pp. 21-22 (broadcast)"
 },
 "notes": [
  "HMS does not appear to host this manual revision publicly any more (newer IN703DAL / INMBSDAL0640200 products have their own manuals); this copy is an unaltered HMS document on an integrator's site (Chipkin).",
  "The manual says every register is a 16-bit signed integer, big endian; levels are whole percent.",
  "The map applies only when the 'Modbus Addresses' parameter in Intesis MAPS is set to Fixed.",
  "For other gear add 100 per short address (sa 0..63), 20 per group (0..15) and 7000 for DALI channel 2 (two-channel model only).",
  "Device-type-specific registers for emergency lighting (type 1, from +42) and LED gear (type 6) exist but are not listed; see the manual.",
  "Addresses 0..20000 that are not in the map are read-only and return 0; an invalid address returns a Modbus exception."
 ],
